  ('1c1c33db-dd31-4b54-8309-0c86169a25e9','Rice Lake Rod & Gun Club in northwestern Wisconsin is organized as a club rather than a commercial range, and like a lot of rod and gun clubs in the upper Midwest, archery is likely one activity among several the organization supports rather than its sole focus. That combined structure, if it holds true here, tends to mean archery access follows the broader club''s membership and scheduling rather than dedicated public hours. This listing doesn''t specify a 3D course, pro shop, or lesson program, so there''s limited detail to go on beyond the name, location, and club-based structure. Anyone interested in archery specifically at this club should contact the organization directly to ask what''s actually available to members and guests.'),
  ('310519c3-f35f-4c24-b2c4-953176561f55','Riceville, a small town in northeastern Iowa, is home to Riceville Archery Club, listed simply as a club rather than a commercial or municipal range. Small-town Iowa clubs like this one are often modest, community-driven setups that run on member involvement rather than advertised hours or a storefront presence, which fits the limited detail available here. There''s no indication of a 3D course, field course, pro shop, or lesson program in this record, so it reads as a bare-bones listing rather than a fully documented facility. For anyone in the area curious about membership, range access, or shooting schedules, contacting the club directly is really the only way to get accurate, current information.'),
  ('7df11c0e-f595-45e1-8f95-fae57d218fca','Rick''s Sporting Goods in Mt. Vernon, Ohio runs a 14-lane indoor archery setup alongside its retail pro shop, a pairing that lets shoppers test equipment or just get practice in without needing a separate range membership. Fourteen lanes is a decent-sized setup for a sporting goods store, suggesting archery is a meaningful part of the business rather than an afterthought tacked onto a hunting and fishing counter. Central Ohio has plenty of bowhunters, and a shop combining retail with range access is a convenient stop for tuning equipment before deer season or just shooting indoors through the winter. This listing doesn''t mention lessons or a 3D course, so confirming those details means checking with the store directly.'),
  ('27ceecae-4251-410b-92d8-d29cf1978010','Kinder, Louisiana is a small town in the southwestern part of the state, and Rider''s Sporting Goods operates there as a commercial business rather than a club, likely serving hunters and outdoor shoppers across a fairly rural stretch of Acadiana. No pro shop flag, lesson program, 3D course, or lane count is attached to this listing, which keeps the available detail limited to the name, location, and general commercial classification. Small-town sporting goods stores in this part of Louisiana often support archery as one piece of a broader hunting and fishing retail operation rather than running it as a dedicated range. Anyone wanting specifics on what archery services or range access this business actually offers should reach out directly.'),
  ('d971324b-da19-43a2-baf4-9bfde152a18d','Farmington Hills, a suburb northwest of Detroit, has its own public archery facility in Riley Archery Range, which as a municipal range is generally open to residents without a club membership requirement. Public ranges of this kind in the Detroit suburbs tend to be simple, maintained by the local parks department, and used by a mix of casual shooters and archers practicing outside club hours elsewhere. This listing doesn''t include lane counts, a pro shop, or any lesson program, which fits the pattern of a straightforward municipal range rather than a full-service operation. Farmington Hills'' own parks and recreation office would be the right place to confirm current hours, rules, and any seasonal closures.'),
  ('386b01a5-f3a0-4391-9f39-4ad8629989b5','Mesa, in the East Valley of the Phoenix metro area, is home to Rio Salado Sportsman''s Club, listed here simply as a club without further detail on programs or amenities. Sportsman''s clubs in the Phoenix area often cover more than one shooting discipline, and archery may be one part of a broader membership offering rather than the club''s sole activity, though this record doesn''t confirm that either way. No 3D course, field course, pro shop, or lesson program is noted, leaving location and general club structure as the main confirmed facts. Given the size of the Phoenix metro archery community, anyone interested in what Rio Salado actually offers for archers should contact the club directly rather than assume.'),
  ('02df323a-c5e6-4fb6-b5af-ac4a00f846ea','Riverside Archers Club, despite its name, is actually located in Ontario, California, a distinction worth noting since it''s easy to confuse with the nearby city of Riverside. It runs as a volunteer club with a field course, meaning targets are set at varied, often uneven distances rather than in a single flat lane, a format that rewards range-estimation skill more than pure flat-target shooting. Southern California''s Inland Empire has a fairly active archery community, and a volunteer-run field course in Ontario gives local shooters an option that doesn''t require driving out to the mountains. No lesson program, pro shop, or 3D course is listed here, so anyone interested should contact the club to confirm access, schedule, and membership requirements.'),
  ('4b27ac33-10c3-4e87-9e06-ad3e96dd3412','Riverside Archery WA in Mount Vernon, Washington operates as a commercial business with an on-site pro shop, putting it in the Skagit Valley north of Seattle where hunting and outdoor recreation are a steady part of local life. Having a pro shop attached to the range means archers can get equipment, tuning, or repairs done in the same visit as their shooting, a convenience that draws both regulars and people just passing through. This listing doesn''t specify lane counts, a 3D course, or lessons, so the pro shop is the one confirmed feature beyond the commercial classification and location. Anyone wanting to know what else the range offers, from course layout to instruction, should contact the business directly.'),
  ('af5f5072-e486-4cda-8fb0-917c9b27ec10','The Woodlands, a planned community north of Houston, maintains Rob Fleming Archery Range as a public facility, which typically means open access for residents rather than a club membership or commercial fee structure. Public ranges tied to master-planned communities like The Woodlands are often part of a broader parks system, built for casual practice rather than competition or full-service instruction. This listing doesn''t note lane counts, a pro shop, or lessons, consistent with a straightforward municipal range rather than a documented full-service facility. The Woodlands Township''s parks and recreation department would be the right contact for current hours, any reservation requirements, and rules for bringing your own equipment onto the range.'),
  ('815cfe00-45a4-4d5e-8bc1-93dbf0f63060','Robertson Archery in Van Nuys, in the San Fernando Valley section of Los Angeles, runs as a commercial operation offering lessons, which makes it a reasonable option for someone in the Valley wanting structured instruction rather than just range access. Los Angeles has a sizable but scattered archery scene, and a commercial range that specifically offers lessons tends to draw people newer to the sport who want guidance before shooting on their own. No mention here of a pro shop, 3D course, or lane count, so those details would need confirmation directly from the business. Given how spread out LA''s archery options are, a lesson-focused range in the Valley fills a specific niche for locals who don''t want to drive across the city.'),
  ('705fedbe-365b-467b-9843-0eb300247d99','Robinson Archery Tucson combines a commercial range with a pro shop, giving Tucson archers a place to shoot and shop for equipment without a second stop across town. Southern Arizona''s desert terrain supports a fair amount of bowhunting, particularly for javelina and mule deer, and a pro shop attached to a range is a practical setup for archers tuning bows or picking up supplies before heading out. This listing doesn''t mention a 3D course, field course, or lesson program, so the pro shop and commercial range status are the two confirmed features here. Anyone in the Tucson area wanting to know about lane availability, hours, or instruction should reach out to the business directly for current details.'),
  ('10e8ea59-9748-4788-b8bd-4e5e7312db5a','Roche-A-Cri Bowman takes its name from the rock formation and state park in central Wisconsin, and while this listing doesn''t specify an exact city, it''s registered as a commercial operation with a 10-target 3D course. A course of that size is enough for a full round of foam-animal target practice, suggesting archery here leans toward bowhunting preparation as much as general recreational shooting. Central Wisconsin has plenty of public land and a strong deer-hunting culture, and a commercial 3D range in that region likely draws hunters tuning up before archery season. No pro shop, lesson program, or exact address is included in this record, so anyone interested should track down the business''s current location and offerings before planning a visit.')
